EXERCISE 11: nslookup
Date: 27. Aug. 2026
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aim: To study and use nslookup for DNS queries and name resolution.
Tools Required: Kali Linux terminal, nslookup utility.
Theory:
nslookup (Name Server Lookup) is a tool for querying DNS servers to obtain domain name
or IP address mapping. It can perform:
 Forward lookup: Domain to IP
 Reverse lookup: IP to domain
 Query specific record types: A, MX, NS, TXT
Procedure:
1. Basic lookup:
nslookup example.com
2. Reverse lookup:
nslookup 93.184.216.34
3. Query specific DNS server:
nslookup example.com 8.8.8.8
4. Interactive mode:
nslookup
> set type=mx
> example.com
> set type=ns
> example.com
> exit
Observation:
Query Type Result
nslookup example.com A 93.184.216.34
nslookup 93.184.216.34 PTR example.com
set type=mx MX 0 .
set type=ns NS a.iana-servers.net
Result: nslookup was used successfully for forward and reverse DNS lookups. Different
record types were queried.